# User runs tests (token contract)

The user runs test commands locally. The agent **does not** run test suites via Shell unless the user explicitly asks (e.g. "run the tests for me").

## Agent behavior

- After code changes, **share commands** for the user to run — do not execute them by default.
- Prefer **targeted** commands (single file / single suite) over full `npm test`.
- Ask for a short result: pass/fail counts, or paste **only failures** / error snippets.
- Do not paste or repeat full test logs unless debugging a specific failure the user shared.

## When the agent may run tests

Only if the user explicitly requests it, or a single minimal check is required mid-fix and the user has not opted out in that turn.

## Command templates (this repo)

```bash
# TypeScript
npx tsc --noEmit

# Unit test (single file)
npx vitest run path/to/file.test.ts

# E2E (single spec)
npx playwright test tests/e2e/your-spec.spec.ts
```

## User reply format (preferred)

One line is enough when green, e.g. `wallEditing 10/10, tsc clean, e2e 2/2`.
